A video frame shown straight from the decoder's memory stays referenced
while the compositor shows it.

With DMA-BUF import the compositor's layer buffer held only duplicated file
descriptors of the frame's memory, not the GstBuffer.  The player drops its
sample as soon as the next frame arrives, the buffer goes back to the
decoder's pool, and the decoder fills that memory with a later frame while
the compositor still draws from it -- frames out of their place in the
timeline, worst on streams with B-frames, and constant when the compositor
lags the player by a frame or two.  The layer buffer now holds the
GstBuffer for its lifetime.

